the realm  do you know what the realm is  it's the thousand blades of aegon's  enemies  a story we agreed to tell each other  over  and over till we forget that it's a lie  what's up ladies and gentlemen welcome  back for another game of thrones season  8 video all right my friends in this  video i want to show you what one of the  game of thrones actors had to say about  the final season of the show during one  of his recent interviews now if you're  like me i think you will find this to be  not only interesting but mostly annoying  because i think it's another attempt at  dismissing at least some of the fans  criticism of game of thrones season 8.  let's have a look at the new article so  i can show you what mr dinklage said  about the final season of game of  thrones the headline reads dinklage says  game of thrones fans were upset about  the finale because they wanted the white  characters to ride off into the sunset  he is basically saying that fans were  only upset because john and danny did  not sit on the iron throne together  that's right he did not hold back in a  recent interview with the new york times  when it was brought up that game of  thrones fans were let down by the show's  finale he also said by the way it's  fiction he added with a laugh there's  dragons in it move on alright now i also  want to give some of my own thoughts on  what he said so far  first off let me just say this i am a  massive fan of the actor not only do i  think he brilliantly brought tyrion  lannister to life on the screen but he  also delivered some of the greatest  scenes in game of thrones i think it's  safe to say that dinklage was one of the  best actors on the show i think he  helped make tyrion one of the most  beloved characters in a cast that was  full of dozens of great actors and  actresses now with that out of the way i  also want to say that i completely  disagree with what he said in the  interview for him to say that fans were  only upset with the finale because the  gorgeous white characters weren't riding  off into the sunset together is simply  false if you go back and watch all of my  older videos you will see that i said  jon snow will never want the iron throne  which made sense because that's who he  was as a character he was never in it  for the iron throne so we would have  been foolish to think that's where he  would have ended now dany on the other  hand has a different story  as we all know daenerys was focused on  taking back king's landing as well as  the iron throne but fans were not angry  just because she didn't get it daenerys  fans were furious because of who her  character became in such a short span of  episodes she basically became adolf  hitler by the end of the series shocking  millions of fans because it seemed to  happen so suddenly they're not angry  because john and danny weren't holding  hands overlooking king's landing in the  end let us also not forget what happened  to the night king now for me this was  the most upsetting and it wasn't only  because zarya stark was the one who  defeated the night king if you have seen  my videos then you know why i think it  was a bad idea to have arya stop the  night king however the other thing that  was so upsetting about this was the fact  that the night king and his army were  defeated almost immediately after they  made it through the wall as you all know  this was something they were building up  since the very first episode of the very  first season then when the night king  finally moves south he's defeated by  someone who didn't even know he existed  before the final season you want to know  what else made a lot of us fans upset  about the final season jaime and cersei  lannister for one we were extremely  unsatisfied with how they died not only  that but i was also heartbroken when i  heard jaime say he never cared about  saving everyone in king's landing it was  already bad enough that he ran back to  cersei but by him saying this it ruins  that amazing scene he had with brienne  when they were bathing in season 3. now  don't even get me started on what  happened in dorne or what happened with  arya stark when she was in braavos  saying that the fans were only angry  because john and danny weren't sitting  on the iron throne is so dismissive our  frustration with the final season goes  way deeper than just this do i even need  to mention how euron greyjoy's character  was handled or how the golden company  was dismantled in seconds i mean the  list of criticisms could go on and on  but i want to go over some of the other  things that he said in the interview  let's go back to when he said by the way  it's fiction there's dragons in it move  on  now just because there were dragons in  the show doesn't mean we should ignore  every mistake the writers made again i  can only speak for myself here but game  of thrones wasn't just some dumb show  that had dragons for me it was much more  than that game of thrones was  groundbreaking in so many ways and in  fact i think it redefined fantasy in a  way that had never been seen on  television before game of thrones had a  vast array of fascinating and complex  characters that blurred the lines of  good and evil even though the show did  have dragons and magic the relationships  the characters had with one another made  them feel real  all of us who did love the show  immediately identified and connected  with a number of different characters  and this made me care about them more  than any other character from different  shows or movies i had ever seen before  everyone else who worked behind the  scenes helped make this show and  universe feel realistic the set  designers the makeup artists the costume  designers the incredible music and so on  and so forth  let's see what else mr dinklage had to  say he said yeah was called game of  thrones but at the end the whole  dialogue when fans would approach me on  the street was who's gonna be on the  throne i don't know why that was their  takeaway because the show was really  more than that dinklage said that one of  his favorite moments from the finale was  when daenerys targaryen's dragon burned  the iron throne because it sort of just  killed that whole conversation which is  really irreverent and kind of brilliant  on behalf of the show's creators he said  shut up it's not about that dinklage  added referencing david benioff and d.b  weiss they constantly did that where you  thought one thing and they delivered  another he said everybody had their own  stories going on while watching that  show but nobody's was as good as what  the show delivered i think  wow he actually thinks no one could have  written it better than what david and  dan did  well once again i disagree  and i would bet that he feels somewhat  different as well but he doesn't want to  go against hbo because i'm sure he would  love to work there again he also said  that he felt audiences were angry about  how the show ended because the show was  simply coming to an end in general  we were going off the air and they  didn't know what to do with their  sundays anymore they wanted more so they  backlashed about that  well my friend we were not the only ones  who wanted more  why is it ending  i don't know ask dave and dan when they  come through um we could have gone to  11 12 13 seasons but uh they i guess  they wanted a life  you wanted it to keep going  well it you know if you've read my  novels  you know there was enough material for  for more seasons they made certain cuts  but but that's fine we have five other  shows five prequels in development  that are based on other periods in the  history of westeros some of them  just a hundred years before game of  thrones some of them five thousand years  before game of thrones  [Music]  [Music]  so  you

